  "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m\u2220A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m\u2220A & ={45}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
